text: "# The BEATS framework — narrative craft for any format\n\nA craft layer that **feeds the format writers.** The agent **finds the story + structures the arc + anchors\nspecifics + tunes emotion/meaning + shapes it to the format**; the **format writers** build the mechanics;\n**WoopSocial publishes**; serialized arcs map into the **content-calendar.**\n\n## B — Begin with the real story\n- Find the **human truth/tension** worth telling: a transformation, a conflict, real stakes. **Not every post\n  is a story** — reserve narrative for content that has one. **Never fabricate** it.\n\n## E — Establish the arc\n- **Setup/problem → turning point → payoff/transformation.** Make the **audience/customer the hero**, the\n  **brand the guide** (StoryBrand). Or BAB / 3-Act / Hero's Journey. Keep it tight — a micro-arc, not a\n  speech.\n\n## A — Anchor in specifics\n- **Concrete sensory detail = believability + resonance.** Replace \"I was stressed\" with the specific scene.\n  **Show, don't tell.** One real detail beats ten generalities.\n\n## T — Tune the emotion + meaning\n- Lead with **one** emotional goal (comfort/pride/relief/belonging). Land the **universal point** they carry\n  away + **see themselves in.** Authentic, not a movie trailer.\n\n## S — Shape it to the format + serialize\n- Compress the arc to the format (**Reel / carousel / post / thread**) → the **format writers**; the **hook is\n  the entry** → `hook-writer`. **Serialize** big arcs into the `content-calendar`. **Measure saves/shares**,\n  not likes. **WoopSocial publishes.**\n\n## The story brief a request should fill\n```\nSTORY: the real tension/transformation (is there genuinely one? if not -> not a story, route to the writers)\nARC: setup/problem -> turning point -> payoff; HERO = the audience/customer, GUIDE = the brand (or BAB / 3-act)\nSPECIFICS: 1-3 concrete sensory details (show don't tell); cut the abstractions\nEMOTION + MEANING: the one feeling; the point they carry away + see themselves in (authentic, not a trailer)\nFORMAT: Reel / carousel / post / thread -> the format writer; the hook -> hook-writer; visual -> image tools/design-and-templates\nSERIALIZE + MEASURE: single or a mapped series (content-calendar); metric = saves/shares/comments. Never fabricate a story.\n```\n\n## Quick structures\n```\nBAB:        Before (the pain) -> After (the better world) -> Bridge (how you get there)\n3-Act:      Setup -> Confrontation/turning point -> Resolution\nStoryBrand: Hero (customer) wants X, faces problem -> meets Guide (brand) with a plan -> success / avoided failure\nTemplate:   \"When [customer] faces [problem], [brand] helps them [outcome] because we believe [value].\"\n```\n"
